From: OpenXPON maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] kbuild: resolve configuration stamps in the kernel object tree

External modules build from their own directory on Linux 6.18. Relative
include/config paths silently drop their Kconfig dependencies there, leaving
objects built with stale options when switching debug profiles.

--- a/scripts/basic/fixdep.c
+++ b/scripts/basic/fixdep.c
@@ -172,7 +172,7 @@ static void use_config(const char *m, int slen)
 		return;
 
 	/* Print out a dependency path from a symbol name. */
-	printf("    $(wildcard include/config/%.*s) \\\n", slen, m);
+	printf("    $(wildcard $(objtree)/include/config/%.*s) \\\n", slen, m);
 }
 
 /* test if s ends in sub */
